<title>UK: U.K. oil output up at 2.5 mln bpd in September.</title>
<headline>U.K. oil output up at 2.5 mln bpd in September.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>British oil production rose by 167,000 barrels per day (bpd) in September from August to 2.5 million bpd as seasonal maintenance work drew to a close, the Royal Bank of Scotland said on Friday.</p>
<p>Gas output in September increased sharply, relecting higher demand from power stations, rising 974 million cubic feet per day (cfd) to 5.765 billion cfd.</p>
<p>Buoyant production and soaring oil prices pushed combined daily U.K. oil and gas revenues to their highest levels in cash terms since 1990, the bank said.</p>
<p>Daily oil and gas revenues climbed by seven million stg to 47 million stg in September, about 25 percent higher than in September 1995.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
